!! Plugin files

|!File |!Role |
|`styles.tid` |All CSS definitions — tagged `$:/tags/Stylesheet` |
|`callout.tid` |Reusable callout box template (info/warning/tip/danger) |
|`notice.tid` |Reusable notice banner template (warning/info/danger/success) |
|`settings.tid` |Settings panel (minimal — no configurable settings) |
|`readme.tid` |Plugin readme with full class reference |
|`icon.tid` |SVG icon |
|`plugin.info` |Plugin metadata |

!! Restart rules

|!Change |!Restart needed? |
|`styles.tid` |Yes — plugin shadow tiddler, requires server restart |
|`callout.tid` / `notice.tid` |Yes — plugin shadow tiddlers |
|Any doc/readme `.tid` |Yes — plugin shadow tiddlers |

<$transclude $tiddler="$:/plugins/rimir/doc-template/templates/callout" type="info">
<$fill $name="body">
Theme has no JS modules — all files are wikitext/CSS shadow tiddlers. "Restart" means restarting the TiddlyWiki server so updated shadow tiddlers are loaded.
</$fill>
</$transclude>

!! Adding new classes

When adding a new `rr-` class:

# Add the CSS rule to `styles.tid` in the appropriate section (tabs, panels, tables, etc.)
# Document the class in `readme.tid` under the relevant subsection
# If the class is part of a reusable pattern (like callouts), consider creating a wikitext template

!! Consuming plugins

Other rimir plugins import theme classes by simply using `class="rr-..."` in their wikitext or by transclusing the callout/notice templates. No import statement or dependency declaration is needed beyond listing theme in `tiddlywiki.info`.

</$fill>
